AMD IP
------

The design uses IP and library elements from AMD (Xilinx). They are not
covered by the Apache License: they stay under AMD's own licence terms (the
licence agreements of Vivado and Vitis 2025.2 and of each IP core).

- IP cores that the Vivado scripts generate: Zynq UltraScale+ MPSoC processing
  system (zynq_ultra_ps_e), AXI DMA (axi_dma), AXI SmartConnect
  (smartconnect), Clocking Wizard (clk_wiz), Processor System Reset
  (proc_sys_reset), Concat (xlconcat), UltraScale FPGAs Transceivers Wizard
  (gtwizard_ultrascale), Soft Error Mitigation (sem_ultra) and In-System IBERT
  (in_system_ibert, IBERT build only)
- the XPM macros (xpm_cdc_*, xpm_fifo_*, xpm_memory_*) and the device
  primitives instantiated in rtl/
- the generated IP files in hpdp_vivado.xpr.zip, and the bitstreams and
  hardware descriptions in build/m7h/hpdp.xsa and build/m7i_1024b/hpdp.xsa

The scripts and RTL of this repository only configure and instantiate these
elements. Building the design needs Vivado and the licences it requires for
the target device.


